For the given problem, since doing bitwise OR makes 1's dominate, we only need to focus on the trees where a leaf node has value 1, as that overrides any other case.

The algorithm to solve this problem is as follows:
1. If either quadTree1 or quadTree2 has a leaf node with value 1, choose that node as the result.
2. If neither quadTree1 nor quadTree2 is a leaf node, perform the bitwise OR for each of the 4 children of the quad trees and save the comparison results.
3. If all children nodes are leaves with the same value, update the current node as a leaf with the common value, otherwise, update the children nodes.

At the end of the recursion, we will have a new Quad Tree representing the bitwise OR of the given binary matrices.

