```
A = A * den + B * num * sign
B *= den
```

After updating A/B, the greatest common divisor (GCD) of A and B, found using the Euclidean algorithm, is used to reduce the fraction.

The process is repeated until the whole string input expression is processed. At the end, the irreducible fraction is returned in the format A/B.

