public int best_rotation(int[] nums) {
    int n = nums.length;
    int[] change = new int[n];

    for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {
        change[(i - nums[i] + 1 + n) % n] -= 1;
        change[(i + 1) % n] += 1;
    }

    int max_score = 0;
    for (int i = 1, cur_score = change[0]; i < n; i++) {
        cur_score += change[i];
        if (cur_score > max_score) {
            max_score = cur_score;
        }
    }
    return max_score;
}
```


    The idea is to calculate the change in score for each rotation instead of recalculating the score every time. We create a `change` array to store the difference in scores when the array is rotated by 1.

For each index `i` in `nums`, decrement the change array value at `(i - nums[i] + 1 + n) % n` by 1 and increment the change array value at `(i + 1) % n` by 1. This will maintain the difference in scores as we perform the rotations.

After that, loop from `i = 1` to `i = n`, updating the `cur_score` by adding the value at `change[i]`. Track the maximum score during the loop.

Finally, return the maximum score.

