public class Solution {
    private static final int MOD = 1000000007;

    public int sumOfWidths(int[] nums) {
        Arrays.sort(nums);
        int n = nums.length;
        long res = 0, c = 1;

        for (int i = 0; i < n; i++, c = c * 2 % MOD)
            res = (res + (nums[i] - nums[n - i - 1]) * c) % MOD;

        return (int) res;
    }
}
```

    1. Sort the given array of integers, nums, in ascending order.
2. Initialize a variable, res, to store the final result, and another variable, c, to keep track of the power of 2.
3. Iterate through the sorted nums array.
4. For each element, calculate the difference between the current element and the corresponding element from the end of the array. Multiply the difference by the current value of c and add the result to res.
5. Update the value of c by multiplying it by 2 and taking the modulo value.
6. Continue this process until the entire nums array has been traversed.
7. Return the final value of res modulo 10^9 + 7.

