public ListNode removeZeroSumSublists(ListNode head) {
    ListNode dummy = new ListNode(0);
    dummy.next = head;
    ListNode current = dummy;

    while (current != null) {
        int sum = 0;
        while (head != null) {
            sum += head.val;
            if (sum == 0) {
                current.next = head.next;
            }
            head = head.next;
        }
        current = current.next;
        if (current != null) {
            head = current.next;
        }
    }

    return dummy.next;
}
```


    We create a dummy node as the initial pointer to keep track of the head of the list. We initialize two pointers, current and head, to the dummy node.

We loop through the linked list while current is not a null pointer. Inside the loop, we also loop through the list while head is not a null pointer. We maintain a sum variable to calculate the accumulated sum of the nodes we traverse. If we encounter a node such that the accumulated sum is zero, we update the next pointer of the current node to the next pointer of head.

Outside the inner loop, we assign current to its next pointer and head to the next pointer of current. We repeat this process until we reach the end of the linked list.

Finally, we return the next pointer of the dummy node, which now represents the head of the linked list.

