Each XOR operation computes the even and odd occurrences for each vowel thus far. It records the first index of the bitmask in the position mapping. The difference between the current index and the value in the position map for the bitmask will give the length of the longest substring with even vowel occurrences. It updates the answer with the maximum substring length found.

