public int minSwaps(String s) {
    int openBrackets = 0;
    int swaps = 0;

    for (int i = 0; i < s.length(); i++) {
        char c = s.charAt(i);

        if (c == '[') {
            openBrackets++;
        } else {
            if (openBrackets == 0) {
                swaps++;
                openBrackets++;
            } else {
                openBrackets--;
            }
        }
    }

    return swaps;
}
```

    The algorithm keeps track of the number of opening brackets '[' encountered while traversing the string. If a closing bracket ']' is encountered and there are no opening brackets available, a swap is required. Thus, the swap count is incremented and ']' is treated as an opening bracket. If there are opening brackets available, a closing bracket ']' can be paired with an opening one so we simply decrement the opening bracket count. At the end, the swap count denotes the minimum number of swaps required to balance the string.

