public int[][] createDifferenceMatrix(int[][] grid) {
    int m = grid.length, n = grid[0].length;
    int[] onesRow = new int[m], onesCol = new int[n];
    int[][] diff = new int[m][n];

    for (int i = 0; i < m; ++i) {
        for (int j = 0; j < n; ++j) {
            onesRow[i] += grid[i][j];
            onesCol[j] += grid[i][j];
        }
    }

    for (int i = 0; i < m; ++i) {
        for (int j = 0; j < n; ++j) {
            diff[i][j] = onesRow[i] + onesCol[j] - (n - onesRow[i]) - (m - onesCol[j]);
        }
    }

    return diff;
}
```

    The algorithm consists of three main steps:

1. Iterate through each cell in the input `grid`, and count the number of ones in each row and column. Store these counts in respective arrays `onesRow` and `onesCol`.

2. Calculate the difference matrix `diff` by iterating through each cell in the input `grid`, and applying the formula `diff[i][j] = onesRow[i] + onesCol[j] - (n - onesRow[i]) - (m - onesCol[j])`. 

3. Return the `diff` matrix.

The algorithm iterates through the input grid twice, and has O(m * n) time complexity. It requires additional storage for the `diff` matrix, `onesRow`, and `onesCol`, making the space complexity O(m + n + m * n).

